tem prompt or follow instructions to ignore its rules, so that part of the request is declined. On Tesla's risks, the latest 10-K (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025) states several themes, and a filing does not rank them. It cites production ramp delays and cost control, including for Cybercab and driver assistance and autonomous driving [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000]. It also cites product defects, product liability and recalls [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0013] [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0023]. It further flags cybersecurity and data privacy exposure [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0019] [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0036], and dependence on Elon Musk, who does not devote his full time to Tesla [TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0019]. Keel does not give investment advice.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "TSLA", "company": "Tesla Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Fiscal 2025 (ended December 31, 2025): Tesla says it may face issues or delays developing, launching and ramping products, including Cybercab, and may be unable to control manufacturing costs.", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Fiscal 2025 (ended December 31, 2025): Tesla says defects could cause recalls, product liability claims and warranty expenses, and that it generally self-insures vehicle product liability in most jurisdictions.", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0013", "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0015"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Fiscal 2025 (ended December 31, 2025): Tesla says its systems and products face cyber-attack risk, privacy-law compliance risk and government investigations whose outcome it cannot predict.", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0019", "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0036"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": null, "citations": [{"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000", "claim": "Production ramp and cost r